// Selling an NFT ticket through an escrow contract. A listed ticket sits in the escrow contract and the listings, and moves to the buyer once paid.
// The amounts are sample values that show the shape.
cards Sell an NFT ticket through escrow

box seller as Seller [note: Aoi]
box escrow as Escrow contract [mark: Held]
box buyer as Buyer [note: Sora]
box market as Listings [mark: Listed]

item t7 as Ticket #7 in seller [amount: 1 NFT, mark: escrow, mark: market]
item u1 as Payment in buyer [amount: 50 USDC]

step List
  say The seller hands the ticket to the escrow contract, and it shows up in the listings.
  seller -> t7: Deposit
  item t7 in escrow, market

step Buy
  say The buyer pays 50 USDC and gets the ticket, and the payment moves to the seller.
  buyer -> t7: Buy
  item t7 in buyer
  item u1 in seller

step Withdraw
  say Once sold, the ticket cannot be withdrawn by the seller.
  refuse t7: Sold tickets cannot be withdrawn
